const passages = [
  {
    "mark": "1986",
    "md": "Born in São Paulo, 1986. My grandparents came from Poland and Romania in 1933, Jews fleeing Nazism. My father taught me that emancipation comes through making. Test the idea in matter before claiming it's good."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2002-2014",
    "sub": "COTUCA · FAU-USP",
    "md": "I studied **Mechatronics at COTUCA** (Unicamp, 2002-04) and **Design at FAU-USP** (2007-14). My thesis, *LUZCIDADE*, traced the lineage from Moholy-Nagy to Dan Flavin and from Flavin to my work with light in São Paulo's public space. Advised by Carlos Zibel Costa, committee included Giselle Beiguelman. I'm not an artist who learned technology. I'm a technician who became an artist. The order matters."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2008-2017",
    "sub": "BijaRi",
    "md": "In 2008 I joined **BijaRi**, where I worked as a VJ and art director for nine years. Live-cinema at Itaú Cultural (2008), video-scenery for Ivete Sangalo at Madison Square Garden (2010), three editions of Villa Mix Goiânia with a Guinness Record for the world's largest LED stage (2013-15). BijaRi taught me to operate at scale."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2017-2018",
    "sub": "GTM Cenografia · The Force",
    "md": "In 2017, at **GTM Cenografia**, I installed the Google Buttonwall in the lobby of Google Brasil with Wesley Lee (about 7,000 interactive RGB buttons) and the scenography of YouTube Space Rio at Pier Mauá (3,000 m², described by G1 as \"the most high-tech in the world\"). In 2018, at **The Force**, I did the technical direction of the *Dimensão* exhibition by Nonotak Studio at Japan House São Paulo."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2019",
    "sub": "AYA Studio",
    "md": "In 2019 Antonio Curti and I began working under the name **AYA Studio**. AYA is a brand we run together, I through **SZT Arte e Tecnologia**, he through **AC Studio**. It is not a company and it is not an artist. It is where the works take on a body, a materialization machine made of people who chose to be there and who recombine with each project. Since then we have worked at Farol Santander, the CCBB centers, Centro Cultural FIESP and Casa Fiat de Cultura. I design the spaces, conceive the works technically and artistically, and direct teams of motion designers, programmers, architects, producers and technicians. Antonio conceives exhibitions and series, writes scripts and signs curatorships. The credits change from work to work because what each of us did changes too: the signature distinguishes responsibility, not value. AYA is the system, and I'm one of its engines."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2019-2023",
    "md": "The first works of this phase still lived inside larger exhibitions. In 2019, in the *Metaversø* show at Farol Santander, [*Mementos*](/en/obras/mementos) sent 45 lasers through a crystal, programmed by Matheus Leston, and [*Interlúdio*](/en/obras/interludio) only lit up when someone came close, with electronics by Wesley Lee. It was the same question in two forms: what is the machine without the body. In 2022, [*Oceanvs*](/en/obras/oceanvs) took up the whole exhibition. Eight acts at Farol Santander, adapted in 2023 for Casa Fiat de Cultura in Belo Horizonte. There I learned to design in collaboration: Antonio's script didn't arrive finished, it changed in the space along with the motion, the score and the programming. Water on the body without wetting the skin."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2023-2024",
    "md": "Then the invisible changed its nature. In [*Metadata: O Mundo Invisível*](/en/obras/metadata) (2023), at Centro Cultural FIESP, it was no longer a buried stream but real-time data from São Paulo disturbing fluids across five screens, an attempt at an X-ray of the city. In [*São Paulo 3024*](/en/obras/sao-paulo-3024) (2024), at Farol Santander, I used language models as a question rather than a tool: is imagining the city a thousand years ahead simulating the future or writing its code? In the same room, the audience's gestures raised buildings that ceased to exist when each person left. These works were signed on the wall by AYA Studio, and the conception is mine. Today I record both things together."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2024-2026",
    "md": "Part of the work is directing so that others can appear. In [*Luz Æterna: Ensaio Sobre o Sol*](/en/obras/luz-aeterna) (2024, CCBB Brasília and CCBB Belo Horizonte), an exhibition conceived and curated by Antonio, eight Brazilian new media artists shared the route, and my job was to let light organize the space without erasing any of them. In [*AMANO: Além da Fantasia*](/en/obras/amano), also conceived and curated by Antonio, I translated 218 original works by Yoshitaka Amano into an immersive room of fifteen laser projectors. The exhibition opened at Farol Santander in 2024 and traveled to the CCBB centers in Belo Horizonte (2025-2026), Rio de Janeiro (2026) and Brasília (2026). In [*O Que Nos Une*](/en/obras/o-que-nos-une) (2025, Centro Cultural FIESP), Miguel Nicolelis's ideas about collective consciousness became mirrors, a floor that tracks position and a room that listens to the heartbeat of whoever enters. In these exhibitions my credit is direction, of art, of technology, of experience."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2025-2027",
    "md": "In 2025 water came back. [*Floresta Utópica*](/en/obras/floresta-utopica), at Farol Santander, takes up the gesture of [*Cachoeira*](/en/obras/cachoeira) thirteen years later: a light sculpture shaped like a waterfall at the center of twenty minutes about the networks between plants, fungi, soil and water. [*Andrômeda: Universo Sem Fim*](/en/obras/andromeda), the same year and at the same Farol, took the scale to the cosmos, with a first room modulated by presence and seventeen minutes of nebulae, supernovae and galaxies. Both belong to the series Os Elementos, which Antonio conceived and curates, and which [*FLAMA*](/en/obras/flama) closes in 2027 with fire: three environments where the visitor contemplates, creates and is revealed by the flame."
  },
  {
    "mark": "2026",
    "md": "In 2026, [*Player 1: 50 Anos dos Videogames*](/en/obras/player1), at Farol Santander, an exhibition conceived and curated by Antonio around Alex Mamed's collection, took the controller out of the hand. In the four experiences I designed, the body is the joystick. It is also the oldest territory of my work, that of someone who built worlds in video games before learning to draw. The same year the work moved inside the machine. I build the engines the pieces run on, and run on local cards, in the studio, everything that fits on them. [*2047: Arquivos do depois de antes*](/en/obras/2047), made with Giselle Beiguelman and shown at Casa Firjan, Rio de Janeiro, in 2026, is where that position becomes explicit, a machine that reads the news about rare earths, writes the future onto continuous paper and publishes its own cost, from the card in the room to the datacenter the writing comes from. The technical research underneath *2047* is published in an open repository, because measuring and showing how the thing works is part of the work."
  },
  {
    "mark": "Publication",
    "coda": true,
    "md": "Years after the thesis, this lineage reappeared explicitly in the book *100 Anos de Arte Moderna: a cena contemporânea*, by Carlos Zibel Costa, the same advisor who accompanied *LUZCIDADE* at FAU-USP. The profile dedicated to my work articulates [*Cachoeira*](/en/obras/cachoeira), [*sem título, para Mantiqueira*](/en/obras/mantiqueira) and [*Oceanvs*](/en/obras/oceanvs) as parts of a single trajectory, from light in public space to the construction of immersive environments."
  },
  {
    "mark": "Lineages",
    "coda": true,
    "md": "My work stands on two lineages. One artistic, from Moholy-Nagy to Dan Flavin, from the light-space modulator to the fluorescent lamp as medium. Another technical, which comes from mechatronics and digital fabrication. The works are born from the intersection of these forces. Revealing the invisible is what persists, from the buried Córrego das Almas in 2012 to the mycorrhizal networks of *Floresta Utópica* in 2025, from a city's data to the ore the machine depends on. What changed is the place of the body. In the first works it watched. Then it became presence that lights up, gesture that builds, heartbeat the room listens to."
  }
];

